   "en": "It was pointed out at the meeting that as far as the next year's economic work is concerned, we must adhere to the principle of pursuing progress while ensuring stability, and boost both quality and performance. We will continue implementing a more proactive fiscal policy and an appropriately accommodative monetary policy, allow full play to the synergies of both existing and newly adopted policies, and bolster counter- and cross-cyclical adjustments so as to tangibly improve the effectiveness of macroeconomic governance. Domestic demand will remain as a focus in building a robust domestic market. It will be essential to enhance innovation-driven development to accelerate the cultivation of new growth drivers. The need was emphasized to deepen reform to boost the momentum and vitality of high-quality development. It will be important to expand high-level opening up for win-win cooperation across multiple sectors. Coordinated development should be advanced for promoting urban and rural integration and integrated regional development. With carbon emissions peaking and carbon neutrality as the goals, efforts will be made to promote a comprehensive green transformation. Prioritizing people's livelihoods, practical measures will be taken to get things done for the people. Red line must never be crossed when it comes to safety, and active and prudent efforts must be maintained to defuse risks in key areas.",
